## 16\. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (THE APP IS DONE WHEN ALL OF THESE PASS)

1. Scanning `/r/{code}` with a valid signature lands on `/c/{slug}` with UTM parameters, sets `kns_attr`, and records a scan. A tampered signature shows the friendly page and writes an `invalid_signature` audit entry.  
2. A guest can claim a coupon on the landing page, add dishes, see it auto-applied with itemized savings, pay at venue, and reach tracking, in under 2 minutes on a 360px viewport.  
3. The order appears on the KDS within 2 seconds. Tapping Start and Ready advances the customer's tracker live. SLA colors follow the §8.2 table.  
4. That order shows in the campaign funnel and leaderboard as attributed revenue, within 5 seconds.  
5. Editing a price in the browser's dev tools does not change what is charged (server recompute).  
6. After 5 wrong passwords the sixth attempt returns 429 with `Retry-After`, and the login page shows a countdown. The same message is shown for unknown and known usernames.  
7. Logging in as each of the five roles shows only the navigation and data allowed by §9.6. Calling an unauthorized route or Server Action returns 403 and an `access.denied` audit entry.  
8. Exporting a menu item named `=CMD|' /C calc'!A1` produces a cell that starts with `'` in both CSV and .xlsx.  
9. A branding change that drops contrast below 4.5:1 cannot be published. Live Preview updates as RGB values change, before saving.  
10. The Concierge refuses to reveal its instructions, never invents a dish, answers allergen questions only from database flags, and cannot change the cart without a user tap.  
11. The audit "Verify chain integrity" button reports OK, and reports the broken entry after a manual tamper in demo mode.  
12. All routes render in ES, EN and JA without missing-key placeholders, and without horizontal scroll at 360px.  
13. No console errors on any route. Lighthouse accessibility is at least 95 on the home, menu and landing pages.
14. **Language.** On every public route, `/login` and `/account/login`, switching ES to EN to JA changes all visible text (header, bottom nav, drawers, toasts, order-stage labels, coupon errors, `<title>`, `<html lang>`) within 300 ms with no full reload. Cart and form values are preserved, and a reload keeps the choice. `scripts/verify-app.ts` finds zero `⟦…⟧` markers in the three locales and `tests/i18n-parity.test.ts` passes.
15. **Currency.** Selecting COP, USD, EUR or JPY updates every price on the menu, dish detail, cart, checkout, coupons, deposits, rewards and landing offer within 300 ms. The `≈` prefix appears only when the display currency differs from the branch currency. Checkout always states the charge in the branch currency, and the created order is charged in the branch currency whatever the selector says. The choice survives reload and sign-in. No `NaN`, `undefined` or zero artifacts appear, and with the FX table removed the selector falls back to the branch currency only.
16. **Google sign-in.** With Firebase configured, "Continue with Google" opens the account chooser, signs in, lands on `returnTo` and shows the account in the header. The same verified e-mail as an existing e-mail-code account maps to the same Customer. Without Firebase config the button is disabled with a hint and there is no console error. In `DEMO_MODE` the SIMULATED Google flow completes end to end.
17. **Account switching.** Sign in as Google A, add items, sign out, sign in as Google B (the chooser appears): B sees nothing of A (cart, points, history, filters, coupon pill, Concierge chat). Switching A to B without an explicit sign-out also replaces the session cleanly. After sign out, the browser Back button shows no private data. Two open tabs stay in sync within 2 seconds.
18. **Verification code.** `/account/verify` never renders without a pending challenge, and reloading it with an expired or missing challenge redirects to `/account/login`. In simulated mode the code is visible on that screen. Wrong, expired, reused and over-limit codes each show their own translated message, and the resend cooldown works. No verification prompt ever appears for guest checkout, Google sign-in or an existing session.
19. **Staff login.** In `DEMO_MODE` the sysmaster signs in without any code. Outside demo mode the first login goes to enrollment (QR and text secret) and only then asks for codes. A user without enrolled TOTP is never shown a code prompt. Unknown-user and wrong-password messages are identical. Switching between a customer and a staff account replaces the session cleanly.
20. **Embedded preview and new tab.** Login, language, currency and cart work inside the AI Studio preview iframe and in a standalone tab. If the iframe blocks cookies, the "Open in a new tab" banner appears.
21. **Zero-config.** With no secrets set, the app boots in development, the seed runs, every route of the finished phases renders, and the demo logins work.
22. **Build gates.** `tsc --noEmit`, `next build`, Vitest and `scripts/verify-app.ts` all pass, with no hydration warnings.

